# SpreadSheetPlus — Project file

> A FreeCAD spreadsheet workbench that **decouples the spreadsheet from the
> parts it drives**. One `MasterSheet` per project holds a configuration table;
> many parts link to it through a lightweight `ConfigRef` and share a named row.
> A parameter change is made once, at the master — and copying a part no longer
> copies the spreadsheet.

## The problem it solves
FreeCAD's built-in Spreadsheet workbench keeps a `Spreadsheet::Sheet` *inside*
the part it drives, so copying a part (or making a link with "copy on change")
copies the sheet too, and the same parameter must be edited in N places. The
built-in "configuration table" binds cells to a part with hidden references,
which has the same coupling.

## How it works
- **MasterSheet** — a document-level `Spreadsheet::Sheet` holding **one**
  configuration table (fixed layout below). Created once per project and
  shareable across files.
- **ConfigRef** — a small `App::FeaturePython` created per part. It links to a
  MasterSheet (same document, or another file via `App::PropertyXLink`) and
  selects one **configuration** (row) by name, exposing that row's
  **parameters** (columns) as read-only properties on the object.
- Parts reference values with ordinary expressions — `ConfigRefA.Length` (or
  `<<ConfigRefA>>.Length`) — never the sheet directly. Switching the row
  (`ref.Configuration = "TypeB"`) re-points every parameter at once.

### Table layout (fixed)
```
             A            B        C        D
1   (title / notes)
2   (label)           Length   Width    Enabled    <- row 2  = parameters
3   TypeA                80      40       True     <- column A = configurations
4   TypeB                85      42      False
```
- Parameter names in `B2`, `C2`, …; configuration names in `A3`, `A4`, …; values
  in `B3…`. Rows/columns are kept contiguous (scans read until empty).

## Key behaviours & decisions
- **Read-through and read-only.** Values live at the MasterSheet; a ConfigRef
  only reads them, and its exposed parameters are read-only in the editor.
- **Two-way editing is rejected** (not deferred): a configuration cell is often
  shared by several parts, so editing it in place would silently change all of
  them. See `PLAN.md` decision 3.
- **Type inference.** A parameter column is exposed as bool / int / float, or as
  a quantity property (`App::PropertyLength`, `Angle`, `Mass`, …) when its cells
  carry units. Unitless numbers act as millimetres in length contexts.
- **Auto re-typing.** A column added while still empty starts as a string and is
  re-typed once values arrive (otherwise sketch constraints fail with
  "Failed to convert to Quantity").
- **Configuration names are case-insensitive** (`TypeA` == `typea`); Switch
  configuration lists them sorted with a case-insensitive type-to-search filter.
- **Containers.** A ConfigRef can live in a `Part`, a `PartDesign::Body` or a
  group — it is created as `Part::Part2DObjectPython`, the only Python-extensible
  type `Body::isAllowed()` accepts.
- **Caching.** `Table.snapshot()` memoises the parsed table by raw cell content,
  so several ConfigRefs sharing one master parse it once.
- **Validation.** `TableSnapshot.problems()` (via `MasterSheet.validate()` /
  `Table.validate()`) reports structural table problems (duplicate parameter
  names, duplicate configuration names, invalid identifier names). Every
  ConfigRef surfaces both scopes in the property editor: `ConfigurationValid` /
  `ConfigurationError` for its own row, `TableValid` / `TableErrors` for the
  master table (including parameters whose name collides with an existing
  property and can therefore not be exposed). A failure also switches the tree
  icon to `spreadsheetplus-config-warning.svg`.
- **The sheet is edited directly.** There is no custom table editor — the
  `MasterSheet` is a plain `Spreadsheet::Sheet` edited in FreeCAD's own
  spreadsheet editor.
- **i18n.** All UI strings go through `i18n.translate("SpreadSheetPlus", …)`;
  compiled `.qm` files live in `resources/translations/`.

## Tech stack
- FreeCAD 1.x / 2.x (AppImages; an extracted copy is used for dev/testing)
- Python 3.11 (bundled with FreeCAD) and FreeCAD's Qt wrapper (`from PySide import …`)
- Namespace workbench layout: `freecad/spreadsheetplus/`
- Addon Manager metadata in `package.xml`

## Repository layout
- `freecad/spreadsheetplus/__init__.py` — headless entry (exports `__version__`)
- `freecad/spreadsheetplus/version.py` — `__version__` (currently `0.1.0`)
- `freecad/spreadsheetplus/init_gui.py` — GUI entry: icons, translations, commands, workbench
- `freecad/spreadsheetplus/workbench.py` — `SpreadSheetPlusWorkbench` (Gui.Workbench)
- `freecad/spreadsheetplus/commands/` — CreateMasterSheet, CreateConfigRef, SwitchConfiguration
- `freecad/spreadsheetplus/dialogs/` — `SelectConfigurationDialog` (row picker)
- `freecad/spreadsheetplus/table.py` — table model + `parse_value` + `TableSnapshot` cache
- `freecad/spreadsheetplus/master_sheet.py` — `MasterSheet` wrapper + `create()`
- `freecad/spreadsheetplus/config_ref.py` — `ConfigRef` proxy (row selection, cross-file link, container support, status flags)
- `freecad/spreadsheetplus/view_providers.py` — `ConfigRefViewProvider` (tree icon)
- `freecad/spreadsheetplus/i18n.py` — `translate()` helper
- `freecad/spreadsheetplus/resources/` — icons, translations, `Resources` manager
- `tests/` — dependency-free FreeCAD test scripts + `run_freecad_gui.sh`
- `docs/` — `usage.md`, `api.md`, `development.md`, `publishing.md`

## Install / dev loop
- Dev (no install): `<freecad> -M <repo-root>`
- Or symlink: `ln -s <repo-root> ~/.local/share/FreeCAD/Mod/SpreadSheetPlus`
- Headless tests: `tests/run_freecad_gui.sh freecadcmd -M <repo-root> tests/<name>.py`
- GUI tests: `tests/run_freecad_gui.sh -M <repo-root> tests/<name>.py`
  (the runner forces the offscreen Qt platform — AppRun sets `xcb` itself, see
  `docs/development.md`).
- Detailed how-and-why: `docs/development.md` (headless running, the AppRun
  `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb` trap, VS Code tasks, where to look in the FreeCAD
  source).

## Dev environment (this machine)
- FreeCAD under test: extracted AppImage at `~/Applications/squashfs-root`,
  version **1.1.3** (`tests/run_freecad_gui.sh` finds it; `FREECAD_APPDIR`
  overrides).
- Full FreeCAD **source checkout**: `~/projects/FreeCad` — on `main`
  (2.x development) but with tags, so read the code of the build under test with
  `git -C ~/projects/FreeCad show 1.1.3:src/...` or
  `git -C ~/projects/FreeCad grep -n <pattern> 1.1.3 -- src/...`.
  Keep it outside this repo: a symlink inside the repo is searchable
  (`search.followSymlinks` is on by default) but puts a few GB of FreeCAD inside
  the addon, where editors/watchers/globs have to walk it — prefer a second
  VS Code workspace folder, or plain `git -C ~/projects/FreeCad show <tag>:<path>`.
- VS Code tasks: *FreeCAD: Run all tests* (headless), *FreeCAD: Test GUI*,
  *FreeCAD: Test container (GUI)*, *Syntax check* — all via the runner.
- **codebase-memory** graph indexes exist for `src`, `src/Gui`, `src/App`,
  `src/Mod/Part`, `src/Mod/PartDesign`, `src/Mod/Spreadsheet` (project names are
  the path with `/` → `-`, e.g. `home-chris-projects-FreeCad-src-Gui`). Use
  `search_graph(query=…)` + `get_code_snippet` + `trace_path` to find code fast;
  `semantic_query` is still broken in 0.10.8 (tested on a fresh full index).
  Every tool also works from the terminal: `codebase-memory-mcp cli <tool> …`
  (handy when a client hides a tool), and the server serves a graph UI on
  port 9749. See `docs/development.md`.

## Notes / decisions
- License: LGPL-2.1-or-later (same as FreeCAD)
- Maintainer: DeveloperChris <github@mailtwister.com>
- ConfigRef parameters are read-only (read-through model): two-way editing is
  deliberately rejected so a naive edit can't silently change other parts that
  share the same configuration cell. Revisit only on user feedback.
- Cell read API (FreeCAD's `Spreadsheet::Sheet` object): use
  `sheet.getContents(address)` for raw cell content; `sheet.get(address)` only
  works for cells exposed as properties (aliases).

