## FreeCAD gotchas (verified)
See `docs/development.md` for how to *run* FreeCAD here; the list below is about
FreeCAD's behaviour.
- FreeCADCmd executes scripts with `__name__` set to the script basename (NOT
  `"__main__"`) — test scripts must call `main()` unconditionally.
- `sys.exit(n)` inside FreeCADCmd propagates the exit code, but Python stdout is
  not auto-flushed — use `print(..., flush=True)` or prints get lost.
- Run scripts with `freecadcmd -M <repo> script.py`, not the bare AppImage
  `python` (which cannot `import FreeCAD`).
- `Sheet.getContents(addr)` returns **string cells with a leading `'` marker**
  (numbers are returned bare). Strip it when reading text.
- `Sheet.set(addr, value)` requires a str; numeric-looking strings become
  numbers, anything else becomes a string.
- `Sheet.removeRows("3", 1)` / `removeColumns("B", 1)` take a 1-based row string
  and a column letter respectively.
- `App::PropertyXLink` links to objects in other documents. Setting it to an
  external object requires the **owner document to be saved first**, otherwise
  it throws "Owner document not saved" (FreeCAD needs the path to compute the
  relative link).
- Do NOT add/remove dynamic properties in a FeaturePython `onChanged` — it fires
  during document restore when external link targets aren't loaded yet, which
  corrupts the exposed properties. Do it in `execute()` (runs on recompute).
- A dynamic property name must not collide with a document object's Python
  attributes (methods like `recompute`) or the FeaturePython `Proxy` property.
  Guard with `hasattr(obj, name)` before `addProperty`, and only sync the
  `ManagedParameters` list in `_sync_values` — never the full parameter list —
  so colliding names are skipped instead of crashing on `getTypeIdOfProperty`.
- A column created while still empty is first exposed as `App::PropertyString`.
  Re-type existing managed properties whenever `infer_type` differs from the
  current property type (only when the column has content), or new columns stay
  string-typed and fail with "Failed to convert to Quantity" in sketch
  constraints.
- FreeCAD containers differ in what they accept. `App::Part` /
  `App::DocumentObjectGroup` take any document object, but
  `PartDesign::Body::isAllowed()` only takes PartDesign features, `Part::Datum`,
  `Part::Part2DObject`, ShapeBinders, `App::VarSet`, `App::DatumElement`,
  `App::LocalCoordinateSystem`; `ViewProviderBody::canDropObject()` additionally
  lets `Part::Feature` through, but dropping one *sets the Body's BaseFeature*.
  A plain `App::FeaturePython` is refused outright. Hence ConfigRefs are
  `Part::Part2DObjectPython`.
- Expression syntax: `<<Something>>.Prop` is a **label** reference; renaming an
  object's label breaks it ("Property 'X' not found in ..."). Use the internal
  name: `ConfigRefA.Length`. Tests use the name form.
- Running the GUI tests: the FreeCAD AppImage's `AppRun` forces
  `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb`, so `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen AppRun freecad …` opens a
  real window and hangs. Use `tests/run_freecad_gui.sh` (replicates AppRun's env
  but keeps offscreen); GUI scripts must close the main window and `sys.exit`
  themselves.
- `pkill -f <pattern>` kills the shell running it when the pattern appears in
  its own command line (e.g. in a VS Code task); use `pkill -f 'squashfs[-]root'`
  or avoid the pattern matching the command itself.
